IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `snap1-logic`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2012a: publicly operated community health centers.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- FORK F-A1: the section applies "the provisions of subsections (f) and (i) of section 2012 ... and section 2019, concerning private, nonprofit drug addiction or alcohol
-- treatment and rehabilitation programs". In this text subsections (f) and (i) of section 2012 are the certification period and the electronic benefit transfer card,
-- which do not concern such programs, and the footnote that explains the letters ("See References in Text note below") points to a note that is not in the text.
-- The text does not choose between "the letters as printed" and "the subsections that concerned the programs when the section was enacted".
-- So the function answers JUST TRUE only for section 2019, and NOTHING for the two letters.

DECLARE `s 2012a provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 2012a subsection (f) of section 2012 as lettered in this text`
    `s 2012a subsection (i) of section 2012 as lettered in this text`
    `s 2012a section 2019`

-- src:137 | Notwithstanding any other provision of law, the provisions of subsections (f) and (i) [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] of section 2012 of this title and section 2019 of this title, concerning private, nonprofit drug addiction or alcohol treatment and rehabilitation programs, shall henceforth also be applicable to publicly operated community health centers.
@ref s 2012a (src:137)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 2012a provision`
      `the provision concerns private, nonprofit drug addiction or alcohol treatment and rehabilitation programs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the center is a publicly operated community health center` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2012a the provision is also applicable to the center` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the center is a publicly operated community health center`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is for "publicly operated community health centers"
        IF NOT `the provision concerns private, nonprofit drug addiction or alcohol treatment and rehabilitation programs`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies the provisions "concerning private, nonprofit drug addiction or alcohol treatment and rehabilitation programs"
        IF provision EQUALS `s 2012a section 2019`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "section 2019 of this title ... shall henceforth also be applicable to publicly operated community health centers"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsections (f) and (i) of section 2012, as lettered in this text, are not about those programs, and the note that explains the letters is not in this text (fork F-A1)
